# TypeScript / TSX style

Apply to `.ts` / `.tsx` in this project. Extend this rule over time; do not invent a parallel style.

## Interfaces and types

- Prefer `interface` for component/object props shapes.
- Name interfaces with an `I` prefix so exports read as interfaces: `IComponentNameProps`, `IUser`.
- Name `type` aliases with a `T` prefix: `TId`, `TThemeMode`.
- Component props interface name matches the component: `ComponentName` → `IComponentNameProps`.

## Naming

- Components: `PascalCase` (`ComponentName`).
- Module-level / exported constants (config, maps, flags): `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` (`MAX_RETRY_COUNT`, `DEFAULT_LOCALE`).
- Do not rename React components or hooks to `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`. Hooks stay `useSomething`; local variables stay `camelCase`.

## Component shape

Prefer this pattern (default export):

```tsx
const ComponentName = (props: IComponentNameProps) => {
  const { name, ...rest } = props

  // ...

  return <View {...rest}>{name}</View>
}

export default ComponentName
```

- Take a single `props` argument typed as `IComponentNameProps`.
- Destructure needed fields from `props` inside the body; put unused/pass-through fields in a rest object (e.g. `rest`), not by redeclaring `props`.
- Use `const` arrow components + `export default` (re-export as named from the slice `index` when needed).

## Comments (JSDoc)

- Components, widgets, screens, and other public UI/modules get a **laconic one-line JSDoc** stating what it is and why it exists.
- The same for key decisions (non-obvious invariants, trade-offs, non-trivial algorithms).
- Local/inline comments while implementing routine features or fixes are **forbidden**, unless they explain critical logic that would otherwise be easy to break.

```tsx
/** Верхняя панель: год, фокус и быстрые статы жизни. */
const LifeTopBar = (props: ILifeTopBarProps) => {
```

## JSX conditionals

- For optional render in JSX prefer `{isTrue && <>...</>}`, not `{isTrue ? <>...</> : null}`.
- Use a ternary only when both branches render real UI (`isTrue ? <A /> : <B />`).

## Preferences

- Library types from dependencies keep their original names (`TextProps`, `StaticScreenProps`, etc.); do not rename imported third-party types with `I`/`T`. Aliases of library types in this project still use the `T` / `I` prefixes (`TStartScreenProps`).
